7) common syntax:-
    $ = hi$            ->hi at end of line
    (hi|bye)ppl |right -> hippl, byeppl , right 
    ^hi                -> start of sentence have hi 
    (ha)-\1,(haa)-\2   -> ha-ha or haa-haa
    [0-9]{2,}          -> 10,2026
    \d                 -> find numbers 
    \D                  -> find non nums
    \w                  -> alnum
    \W                  -> except alnums
    \s                   -> find space
    \S                   -> excep space 
    \b                   -> match from clean new word 
    ?                   ->  optional match to the left(0 or more )
    ?=                  -> positive lookahead( what we want should be succedded by whom?)  use () to grp 
    example: \d+(?=PM)  ->  Date: 4 Aug 3PM, 3PM matches only. 
    ?!                  -> match except the string following it 
    example: \d+(?!PM)  -> Date: 4 Aug 3PM, 4 matches only. 
    ?<=                 -> lookbehing 
    example: 1)(?<=\$)\d+ -> Product Code: 1064 Price: $5 , matched $5
